     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>Le mardi 31 mars 2015 16:14:31 UTC+2, Joe Cheng [RStudio] a écrit :<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><p dir=\"ltr\">You have to have shinyApp as the last line; it needs to be the thing that&#39;s returned when Shiny calls source() on your file.</p>\r\n<div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Mar 31, 2015 4:31 AM, &quot;Jean-François Moyen&quot; &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">jfm...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br type=\"attribution\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<br><br>More experimenting with Shiny... I was willing to try the &quot;single file&quot; approach, as per<br><a href=\"http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/function.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/function.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792388077432000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ifvWZ8dQnhOP2msb1QqP2\">http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/function.html</a><br><br>I have the following minimum function, borrowed from<br><a href=\"https://github.com/rstudio/shiny-examples/tree/master/084-single-file\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/rstudio/shiny-examples/tree/master/084-single-file&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792388077432000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1kqkI3T4bY9dSumKC2fPCC\">https://github.com/rstudio/shiny-examples/tree/master/084-single-file</a><br><br>__________________________________________<br>shiny_test.r<br>------------------------<br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#008\">require</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;shiny&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color